1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,255
Nobody taught this robot how to jump.

2
00:00:02,395 --> 00:00:03,523
No motion capture.

3
00:00:03,663 --> 00:00:04,973
Just one nose camera.

4
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:08,325
Yet it vaults concrete walls taller than its body,

5
00:00:08,445 --> 00:00:09,994
even in pitch darkness.

6
00:00:10,174 --> 00:00:13,053
It crawls flat under twenty-centimeter gaps,

7
00:00:13,173 --> 00:00:17,124
and tilts onto two legs through slits narrower than its shoulders.

8
00:00:17,324 --> 00:00:19,913
Most robots learning stunts like this crash thousands of times,

9
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:22,748
stopped cold by solid walls.

10
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:26,360
So Stanford and Carnegie Mellon engineers broke physics first.

11
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:30,932
For twelve hours in simulation, they turned walls into ghosts.

12
00:00:31,092 --> 00:00:32,935
It walked straight through barriers,

13
00:00:33,055 --> 00:00:36,059
but paid a penalty for every millimeter of overlap.

14
00:00:36,259 --> 00:00:41,177
To escape it, the AI invented climbing, crawling, and tilting on its own,

15
00:00:41,317 --> 00:00:44,841
before six hours of real physics locked those instincts in.

16
00:00:45,061 --> 00:00:47,780
Outdoors, something eerie emerged.

17
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:50,053
When a brick wall stops it cold...

18
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,290
Nobody coded a retry,

19
00:00:52,410 --> 00:00:55,006
yet it shoves off the stone for run-up space,

20
00:00:55,126 --> 00:00:57,170
and clears the ledge on the second charge.

21
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:57,966
Remember...
